# companion.conf — instance config for the companion-mac comms fabric
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COPY this file to `companion.conf` (same dir) and fill it in.
# `companion.conf` is gitignored — it is YOUR private instance.
# The whitelabeled scaffolding (this .example, lib/, services/_template/)
# is public; only the populated instance is private.
#
# Sourced as bash. Keep it to KEY="value" and arrays. No secrets that
# would be catastrophic to leak still belong here (tokens, keys) — those
# live in each service's own gitignored env, never in this file.

# ── Identity of the companion machine ───────────────────────────────
# Prefer a stable SSH-config alias or a Tailscale MagicDNS name over a
# bare `.local` mDNS name — `.local` dies the moment the two machines are
# on different networks, which is exactly when you need to reach it.
COMPANION_HOST="companion.local"      # display/reference name
COMPANION_SSH_ALIAS="companion"       # `ssh <alias>` — set this up in ~/.ssh/config
COMPANION_USER="youruser"
COMPANION_WORK="/Users/youruser/work" # remote work root (absolute — SSH lands in ~)

# ── Local side (this machine) ───────────────────────────────────────
LOCAL_WORK="$HOME/work"
COMMS_DIR="$LOCAL_WORK/comms"          # the Syncthing-shared comms folder
QUEUE_DIR="$COMMS_DIR/queue"           # mirrored queue root (file-drop bridge)

# ── Liveness ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
HEARTBEAT_MAX_AGE=300                  # seconds; a heartbeat newer than this = "up"

# ── Services to scaffold queues for ─────────────────────────────────
# Each name N gets QUEUE_DIR/N-inbox, N-outbox, N-processed created.
# These are just folder names — the actual workers are private plugins
# you build from services/_template/.
SERVICES=(example)
